  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nOngoing quiet weather pattern holds steady through the work week\namid high pressure anchored over the region. Mid-level cloud\ncoverage early this morning denotes a passing shortwave, but\nposes little to no chance for precipitation during its brief\nresidency. While upper level ridging gradually compresses\nthrough the course of the week into the start of the weekend,\ndry weather and above normal temperatures will prevail.\n\nThe return of rain chances opens up the month of November on\nSunday, as a southern stream disturbance tracks into the Ohio\nValley. While initial accumulations progged for the end of the\nweekend look low, this feature will set off an unsettled weather\npattern that will stretch into the start of next week. Timing and\nextent of this approaching disturbance will continue to be \nhashed out as we get closer to the weekend timeframe.",
